course: dictionary
lesson: 3191
title: Endangered: in danger of dying out
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: An endangered animal or plant is one that may soon die out completely because very few are left. Read the clues around the word. «Orangutans live only on Borneo and Sumatra and are critically endangered, as their forest is cut for timber and palm oil.» The words only, cut and forest tell you the orangutans have little space left, so endangered means in serious danger of dying out.
explain: Endangered can also mean put in danger. Look at the verb endanger: it means to put someone or something at risk. «Protecting bamboo forests in China helped giant pandas, which moved from endangered to vulnerable in 2016.» Here endangered means the pandas were at great risk, and vulnerable means still at risk but less so.
explain: Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. «About 7,000 languages are spoken today, and nearly half are endangered.» Does "nearly half are at risk of dying out" make sense? Yes, so you have found the right meaning.
fact: Endangered means at risk of dying out completely.
fact: Endanger is a verb. Its past form is endangered, as in «hunting endangered the sea turtles».
fact: Endangered species include tigers, pandas, orangutans, sea turtles and kakapos.
fact: Main causes are loss of habitat, hunting, pollution and climate change.
fact: «Critically endangered» means in the most serious danger of dying out.
exercise: «Orangutans live only on Borneo and Sumatra and are critically endangered.» What does critically endangered suggest? | They are the fastest animals on Earth | Many are living happily in every country | They live in the ocean | *Very few are left and they may soon die out
exercise: «Giant pandas moved from endangered to vulnerable, still at risk but less so.» What does vulnerable mean here? | Put in danger by a storm | Very hungry | *Still at risk, but less so | Completely safe for ever
exercise: Hunting and pollution can endanger animals. What does endanger mean? | Feed and care for | Count and record | Save from danger | *Put in danger
test: «About 7,000 languages are spoken today, and nearly half are endangered, because children grow up speaking a bigger language instead.» What does endangered mean in this sentence? | Written down in a book | *At risk of dying out | Spoken by everyone in the world | Very loud and clear
test: In the past, hunting ___ the sea turtles. Which word fits best? | *endangered | endangers | endangering | endanger
exam: «In 2016 giant pandas moved from endangered to vulnerable, because China protected bamboo forests and made corridors between them.» Why did the pandas improve? | *Their forests were protected and wild numbers grew | They learned to fly | The bamboo forests were cut down | People stopped visiting zoos
